# nr-office-design-templates: what the wiring applies for the templates module of mixdog-office-design.
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change: the module is pure functions and has no caller yet.
#  No new crate and no new dependency edge: the module uses mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml, mixdog-rt,
#  which crates/mixdog-office-design/Cargo.toml already lists. Cargo.lock and the workspace hack need no change.)

# 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-design/src/lib.rs, after the line `pub mod library;` add:
pub mod templates;

# 2. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, "sets" (keep the list sorted by set name; after "office-tabular" or wherever
#    "office-templates" falls):
    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-templates.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-templates/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "025272f4169408426b19b68613740b055be899d9fb91e88c6ea58d42215e44d5",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-templates.mjs",
      "set": "office-templates",
      "totalBytes": 2695047
    },

# 3. For the callers of the design library (nr-office-design-library's `Context`): pass `&templates::OfficeTemplateIndexer`
#    as `Context::indexer` (it is the `TemplateIndexer` that `indexOfficeTemplates` is). `templates::index_office_templates`
#    and `templates::inspect_office_template` are the direct forms.

# 4. For the porters of src/runtime/office/core/office-actions-batch.mjs and office-sessions.mjs:
#    - `templates::expand_template_page_operations(proof, format, &operations, &mut carriers, &mut snapshot)` is
#      `expandTemplatePageOperations`; `snapshot(path)` must answer `snapshotPortableOoxml(path, 'pptx')` (the deck snapshot
#      reader of the pptx port, which this module does not own); the fill reads the sidecar `<path>.mixdog.json` itself.
#    - `templates::create_pptx_slide_selection(lane, source, &slides, output)` is `createPptxSlideSelection` (the
#      `replace_slides` batch source).
#    - `templates::annotate_pptx_snapshot_roles(&mut document)` is `annotatePptxSnapshotRoles` (office-sessions snapshot read).
#    - `templates::select_template_page` and `templates::template_page_fill` are the page choice and the fill.

# 5. Packaging: the packaged templates sit in crates/mixdog-office-design/assets/templates (mixdog-executive.pptx,
#    mixdog-executive.mixdog-edit.pptx, mixdog-executive.pptx.mixdog.json, copied byte for byte from
#    src/runtime/office/design/library/templates). `Environment::process()` reads them from `assets/templates` beside the
#    executable, so the packaging task that ships the Rust runtime copies that folder next to it.
